course: dictionary
lesson: 4400
title: Haitian: a place, a people, a language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. «Haitian» is one of them. It tells you that something is from Haiti, or belongs to Haiti.
explain: Look at the words around it: «The Haitian Revolution from 1791 overthrew slavery in the French colony of Saint-Domingue, and Haiti became independent in 1804.» Haitian comes before Revolution, and the sentence is about Haiti, so Haitian means to do with Haiti.
explain: Haitian can also be a noun. «Haitians» are people from Haiti. A Haitian is one person from Haiti. The same word can name a people, a language or a kind of food, so the words beside it tell you which one it means.
fact: Haiti is a country in the Caribbean, on the island of Hispaniola.
fact: «Haitian» can be an adjective, as in «Haitian food», or a noun, as in «a Haitian».
fact: «Haitian Creole» is the language most people speak in Haiti, together with French.
fact: Haiti became independent in 1804, after the Haitian Revolution from 1791.
exercise: Which word means a person from Haiti? | Creole | *Haitian | Hispaniola | Caribbean
exercise: «Haitian Creole» is the language most people speak in which country? | Brazil | Japan | *Haiti | Ethiopia
exercise: The Haitian Revolution made Haiti independent in which year? | 1910 | *1804 | 1791 | 1492
test: In «Haitian food», what does Haitian mean? | *From or to do with Haiti | A dish | Very old | Dangerous
test: Haiti is on which island? | Ireland | Jamaica | Cuba | *Hispaniola
exam: Which sentence uses Haitian as a noun, meaning a person? | «Haitian food is tasty.» | *«Many Haitians live in the towns and cities.» | «Haitian Creole grew from French and African languages.» | «The Haitian Revolution began in 1791.»
